<%# Port of the legacy SPA `Hujah/pinned.js` — signup CTA shown to logged-out visitors.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.4) —
    docs/design-system/components/social/PinnedCTA.prompt.md: "the one place Hoojah uses
    purple as a fill. Copy is verbatim … Colours are fixed (disagree purple card, agree
    orange button); do not retint it." Both halves of that are load-bearing and both are
    left alone: `bg-disagree` / `bg-agree` are not decoration to be harmonised with the
    surrounding indigo, and the two sentences are frozen strings.

    The button becomes `ds_button_classes(variant: :rect, tone: "agree")` — VISUAL
    FOUNDATIONS puts "rect `rounded` solid buttons on auth screens & the signup CTA",
    and this is that CTA. `tone:` is what carries the orange; the `rect` variant itself
    is colourless. %>
<div class="shadow bg-disagree text-white mb-2 p-4 text-center">
  <h5 class="font-medium mb-3">Create a Hoojah account<br>to secure your @username now!</h5>
  <%= link_to "Click here to sign up!", new_user_registration_path,
        class: ds_button_classes(variant: :rect, tone: "agree") %>
</div>
